# Domain Rules

Status: DONE
Milestone: M1 Technical proofs
Dependencies: `01_PROJECT_FOUNDATION.todo`, accepted territory decisions in `15_PRODUCT_DECISIONS.todo`

## Purpose

Implement deterministic game rules without Unity scene or rendering dependencies.

## Tasks

- [x] Define element, owner, territory state, player ID, team ID, and match phase value types.
- [x] Define logical territory cell and field interfaces.
- [x] Define data-driven reaction rule model.
- [x] Implement Ice, Fire, and Mist conversions for the slice.
- [x] Define score and coverage calculation.
- [x] Define bank award policy.
- [x] Define match timer and phase transitions.
- [x] Define explicit tie and zero-ownership behavior.
- [x] Define seedable randomness abstraction.
- [x] Validate configuration at construction/bootstrap.
- [x] Add comprehensive domain unit tests.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Domain assembly has no `UnityEngine` reference.
- [x] Every in-scope conversion has positive and negative tests.
- [x] Fixed stamp sequence produces deterministic coverage and bank.
- [x] Invalid configurations fail with actionable errors.
- [x] Domain tests run without opening a Unity scene.

## Completion evidence

- Pure-C# implementation under `EntropyTag/Assets/EntropyTag/Scripts/Domain/`.
- Domain assembly retains `noEngineReferences: true` and source contains no Unity API references.
- EditMode: 24 passed, 0 failed.
- PlayMode regression: 10 passed, 0 failed.
- Windows development build succeeded.
- Fixed 2x2 stamp sequence deterministically produces Ice 1, Fire 2, Neutral 1, Mist 0, and Fire bank 3.
- Documentation: `docs/12_DOMAIN_RULES.md`.
- Developer review approved.

## Completion log

- 2026-08-21 - Implemented validated IDs, territory cells/field interfaces, first-slice reaction configuration,
  CPU-authoritative stamping, coverage and winner resolution, bank awards, two-minute match phases, seeded
  randomness, and comprehensive domain tests. Automated validation passed and the developer approved the
  rule package.
